On 7 May 2010 19:08, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:

> How would you say "john understands english" in lojban, xorxes?  (And {la
> djan se bangu le glibau} says that he uses it, not that he understands
> it/knows it).
>

"John understands English" means that something can be communicated to John
by means of English. And this is what {la djan se bangu le glibau} means, is
it not? Being capable of understanding a language is being capable of using
a system of words in interpreting information encoded with that system. If
by "use" you mean an actual application of the ability, that's something to
be made explicit with {ca}, {ca'a}, etc.

